# The Ada program GNAT builds on CuBit (tests/gnat): it writes its
# transcript to standard output (its unix.stdout outlet, which the test
# reads) and to transcript.txt in the work place, which the test delegates
# to it. ccl-manifest renders this as assembly (hello-manifest.s), which
# the gcc driver assembles and links on CuBit with the program.
(Executable_Manifest
  identity => "com.cubit.gnat-hello"
  version => "0.1.0"
  requests => [(service "filesystem" "filesystem")]
  outlets => [
    (Outlet "unix.stdout" Element.Text pages => 4)
    (Outlet "unix.stderr" Element.Text pages => 4)]
  descriptors => [(Descriptor 1 "unix.stdout") (Descriptor 2 "unix.stderr")])
